{"id": "EUVD-2026-81962", "enisaUuid": "c077af2c-f48d-306b-9e64-e2cf83bc9b18", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbnxt_en: Fix call to hardware monitoring event handler\n\nThe first parameter of hwmon_notify_event() is supposed to be the hardware\nmonitoring device. The bnxt driver calls it with the platform device as\nfirst parameter instead. This API break results in undefined behavior and\nmay result in a crash.\n\nPass the hardware monitoring device as parameter instead to fix the\nproblem.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3cad8389a72b8a309b5689c1683310126b0d7da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/001ff5d8e68aacd91768b824b930dd7e68db6688", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b17907ef665bc76a495a8f909f74656d3f32b7a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/622d698df4239fef3e0eb51fe59f4198f957f28a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vwp5-jm9v-mqjg", "CVE-2026-90101"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0de17e43-fa53-3ab0-945a-99618d35d1ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a19b4801457b0806c0153dc344f548c6f8615896 <e3cad8389a72b8a309b5689c1683310126b0d7da"}, {"id": "17bc7ab8-87e0-3f3b-9e27-f4b6e3730202", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "6b201df6-c258-3dce-8337-7ca3db8125b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a19b4801457b0806c0153dc344f548c6f8615896 <622d698df4239fef3e0eb51fe59f4198f957f28a"}, {"id": "824384ac-8020-35e6-9e7d-5809687dd611", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a19b4801457b0806c0153dc344f548c6f8615896 <b17907ef665bc76a495a8f909f74656d3f32b7a2"}, {"id": "9045d021-f8ea-30f6-9cde-099c7cb0d0fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"